    "body": "2026 Paris Motor Show • The Volkswagen Group's Affordable BEV Quartet Has Almost Reached 150,000 Orders\nS650 Ford Racing Mustang Cobra R Takes the new Mustang Dark Horse SC in a Virtually Crazy Direction\n9 photos\nPhoto: abimelecdesign / Instagram\nThe Ford Motor Company has crafted a few new and cool models for the iconic Ford Mustang lineup – the 795-horsepower Dark Horse SC and 815-hp Mustang GTD being chief among them. While we wait to see if the Blue Oval also adds a new sedan body style, let’s also imagine something else thanks to a member of the imaginative guild of digital car content creators dwelling across the parallel universes of vehicular CGI.\nAbimelec Arellano, a virtual artist better known as \" abimelecdesign \" on social media, has prepared the newest wishful-thinking project - a cool American coupe. The thing is that this pixel master has a knack for the Blue Oval side of America’s automotive market. He recently gave us a Ford Taurus SHO Saleen sedan, a Ford Crown Victoria Ute with steelies, and even a Ford Crown Victoria with an Australian passport, among others.\nBut now he’s not interested in sedans – only feisty muscle cars of the coupe variety. He explains that he thinks the “new Mustang Dark Horse SC is incredible— 2.9 seconds to 60 and a bunch of track-ready hardware, plus a very distinctive body kit and aerodynamics. I love that, and I love it even more because underneath the Dark Horse badges, carbon fiber wheels and carbon fiber inserts, I can see something else that had been missing from Mustangs for a while,” aka the ‘Cobra stance.’\nAccording to his vision, the Cobra models from the Ford Motor Company from the 1990s and 2000s “had a very unique stance— whether you’re talking about the Fox-bodies or the more extreme Cobra Terminator, they always had that ‘chunkier,’ heavier, aggressive presence.” So, when Ford unleashed the 795-hp Dark Horse SC, “the overall look just screamed Cobra stance to me, more specifically, one of the most iconic Mustangs of all time: the 2000 Cobra R .”\nAs such, he decided to bring out the “essence” of that model to CGI light, via some digital modifications plastered over the Dark Horse SC: “the chin spoiler is deeper, lower, and the side aero elements are gone. The carbon fiber inserts are all painted, along with replacing the grille horse with the Cobra.” Additionally, the artist reimagined the five-spoke Cobra R wheels, created thicker and lower side exhausts, and now there are side exhausts, of course.\nLast but not least, the CGI presentation is based on the “wonderful” Need for Speed: Hot Pursuit 2 video game, and the “rear diffuser is hollowed out where the exhausts used to be to move more air, and on top of the rear sits the controversial Cobra R wing. Of course, it is not exactly a Cobra R wing; this is way more curved and contoured to the body of the S650, but keeps the styling almost identical to the original.” View this post on Instagram A post shared by Abimelec Arellano (@abimelecdesign)\nLiked the article? Follow us to see more articles from autoevolution in your Google feeds.\nS650 Ford Racing Mustang Cobra R Ford Mustang Ford Mustang Cobra R CGI revival rendering abimelecdesign\nAbout the author: Aurel Niculescu\nAurel has aimed high all his life (literally, at 16 he was flying gliders all by himself) so in 2006 he switched careers and got hired as a writer at his favorite magazine. Since then, his work has been published both by print and online outlets, most recently right here, on autoevolution. Full profile\nUP NEXT Meet the Carbon Fiber Beast: The Ultimate One-of-One Mansory P820 Linea D’Arabo",
